{"name":"Mammoth Mountain","hex":"#3b6a7a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Mammoth Mountain","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A volcanic area in California, USA."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mammoth_Mountain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mammoth Mountain","blocks":[{"text":"Mammoth Mountain is a lava dome complex partially located in the town of Mammoth Lakes, California, within the Inyo National Forest of Madera and Mono counties. It is home to a large ski area primarily on the Mono County side."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Ritter_Range_and_Mammoth_Mountain.jpg/330px-Ritter_Range_and_Mammoth_Mountain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mammoth_Mountain","wikidata":"Q953984"},{"title":"Mammoth","blocks":[{"text":"A mammoth is a member of the extinct elephantid genus Mammuthus. They lived from the late Miocene epoch into the Holocene until about 4,000 years ago, with mammoth species at various times inhabiting Africa, Asia, Europe and North America. Mammoths are distinguished from living elephants by their spirally twisted tusks and in some later species, the development of numerous adaptions to living in cold environments, including a thick layer of fur."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Mammuthus_columbi_Page.jpg/330px-Mammuthus_columbi_Page.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mammoth","wikidata":"Q36715"},{"title":"Mountain","blocks":[{"text":"A mountain is an elevated portion of the surface of a planet, generally with steep sides that show significant exposed bedrock. Although there are no universally accepted definitions, a mountain is usually considered higher than a hill. By definition, mountains are often thought of as being a landform which is higher than 2,000 feet (610 m). It may either have a limited summit area or be a smaller plateau with high elevation and steep sides. A few mountains are isolated summits, but most occur in mountain ranges."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg/330px-Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain","wikidata":"Q8502"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Death_by_Carbon_Dioxide%2C_Horseshoe_Lake%2C_Mammoth%2C_CA_2016_%2832011250720%29.jpg/500px-Death_by_Carbon_Dioxide%2C_Horseshoe_Lake%2C_Mammoth%2C_CA_2016_%2832011250720%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Death_by_Carbon_Dioxide%2C_Horseshoe_Lake%2C_Mammoth%2C_CA_2016_%2832011250720%29.jpg/1280px-Death_by_Carbon_Dioxide%2C_Horseshoe_Lake%2C_Mammoth%2C_CA_2016_%2832011250720%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Death_by_Carbon_Dioxide%2C_Horseshoe_Lake%2C_Mammoth%2C_CA_2016_%2832011250720%29.jpg/500px-Death_by_Carbon_Dioxide%2C_Horseshoe_Lake%2C_Mammoth%2C_CA_2016_%2832011250720%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Overabundance of carbon dioxide in the soil from a natural underground volcanic source has killed a large area of trees","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADeath_by_Carbon_Dioxide%2C_Horseshoe_Lake%2C_Mammoth%2C_CA_2016_(32011250720).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Mammoth_Mtn_ski_area_%2816126219736%29.jpg/500px-Mammoth_Mtn_ski_area_%2816126219736%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/